  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $y=x+1 \\text { and } y=\\cos x$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2019_mat_a68.png\">\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\text { Require area } &=\\int_{-1}^{0}(x+1) d x+\\int_{0}^{\\pi / 2} \\cos x d x \\\\ &=\\left[\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+x\\right]_{-1}^{0}+[\\sin x]_{0}^{\\pi / 2} \\\\ &=\\left[(0)-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}-1\\right)\\right]+[1-0] \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{3}{2} \\text { sq unit. } \\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
